.TH "CSSMATHINVERT.CSSMATHINVERT" "3JS" "August 7, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSMathInvert.CSSMathInvert \- CSSMathInvert: CSSMathInvert()
constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSMathInvert()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] object which represents the inverse
(reciprocal) of a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSMathInvert(arg)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]arg\f[R]
A number or \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R] that represents the value to
invert.
.SS Exceptions
None.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following code creates a \f[CR]CSSMathInvert\f[R] object from a
percentage, then logs the constructor name, \f[CR]value\f[R], and the
object\(cqs serialization (from \f[CR]toString()\f[R]).
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] inverted = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSMathInvert(CSS.percent(4));

console.log(inverted.constructor.name); \f[I]// \(dqCSSMathInvert\(dq\f[R]
console.log(inverted.value); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 4, unit: \(dqpercent\(dq}\f[R]
console.log(inverted.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqcalc(1 / 4%)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Note that if a plain number is passed to \f[CR]arg\f[R], the
\f[CR]value\f[R] is rectified to a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] with unit
\f[CR]\(dqnumber\(dq\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] invertedNumber = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSMathInvert(4);

console.log(invertedNumber.value); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 4, unit: \(dqnumber\(dq}\f[R]
.EE
